--TEST--
a `string|tainted string` is refused wherever the bare `tainted string` is -- a sink, a contagious answer with nowhere to put the bit, and the plain type a contagious call does not answer -- so admitting the union arm by arm launders nothing -- `rule:security/unclassified-parameter-refuses-tainted`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The other half of `a-union-carrying-tainted-reaches-every-mark-that-admits-it`.
// Reaching into a union is a narrowing of the *admission*, so the three places
// that refuse an atom have to refuse the union too, or the reach would be a
// laundering hole rather than a spelling.
?tainted string $configured = Core\Env::get("NVS_CASE_UNSET_ORIGIN");
var $chosen = $configured ?? "host.example";

// `Core\IO::within`'s `$base` is `Qual::Sink`: no reach applies at a mark that
// admits nothing, and one tainted arm is enough to refuse the whole union.
string $resolved = Core\IO::within($chosen, "child.txt");

// `Core\Uri::parse` is contagious and answers an instance, which has no cell to
// carry the qualifier -- `rule:security/unclassified-parameter-refuses-tainted`'s deliberately conservative half, which
// the union reaches no further into than the atom did.
Core\Uri $uri = Core\Uri::parse($chosen);

// And the contagion the admission implies is really set: `decodeComponent`
// takes the union, so its answer is `tainted bytes` and not the `bytes` its
// row declares. This is the line that would silently pass if `carries_contagion`
// asked the atom question about a union.
string $decoded = Core\Uri::decodeComponent($chosen);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `string|tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:11:36
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `string|tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:16:33
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted bytes`
   --> case.nvs:22:19
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
